I don't get why so many people buy an early-access game, then complain about it not being finished and having bugs. The updates come frequently, the developers are actually interested in what the players want and prioritize new features / fixes based on that and there's an exploit hunting program in place, so all problems will eventually get fixed. As long as you know that you're not getting the finished product and you're willing to experiment, see what can be done and all the possibilities being offered, then you'll have fun playing.
Pros:
- large world to explore, with almost everything around wanting to kill you;
- the construction aspect is quite great, despite it not being completely finished just yet and the fact that you have to make sure that your structures are supported is interesting;
- the thrall hunting is quite fun, making you constantly search for new and better people to have working in your structures;
- the survival aspect makes the game more realistic.
Cons:
- the multiplayer aspect isn't very good yet: the PVP system (two players fighting against one another) is not very interesting / skill-based;
- pretty hard to find good spots to build your base that aren't already occupied by other players;
- the default settings, (the ones you will encounter on official servers) make the game a real grind-fest and hackers will screw you over from time to time;
- mods get messed up constantly by new updates and because of how the system is implemented they may cancel each other out as in two or more mods, may not work together even though they add/modify diffrente things.
In my experience so far, the best way to play Conan exiles is on a private server just for you and your friends. The ability to modify the harvest rates will ensure that you don't need to spend hundreds of hours building a higher tier base and modifying the damage values could help you explore the entire map without needing a bunch of friends to defeat dragons or rhino kings.

Still not finished, but I've had enough.
Pros:
+ Very, very funny level design, with the most complex and amazing exploration mechanics in the Prince of Persia franchise;
+ Secondary abilities, very useful in combat, adding depth to the choice (and level up).
... and that's all, because as Cons:
- Combat system is shallow per se, nothing matches the amazing work of Warrior Within and alas, this came after that and is worse (also, enemies variety is ridiculous: how many types are there, like, 4?);
- Camera often misleading the player to die even if not at fault - Ubisoft, it's not the first time!;
- Bosses also quite shallow, no need to make up strategies: just slash them until they fall;
- UPlay. I guess that's the answer to this awful bug: every once in a while, I started the game and waited in front of a neverending black loading screen. Process was stuck, not answering. Unable to start the game. It could even be a decent game, if the experience was not ruined by this bug. Oh, how many times I had to reinstall all the damn thing and it still didn't work. Warrior Within is much better, if you can cope with crappy textures and resolution.
